<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 6 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Rebels against Empire</h1><p class="path-tagline">Six risings against the greatest powers of their age.</p><p class="path-intro">Every empire in this collection was defied by someone who refused its terms. This path follows six of them, enslaved and royal, doomed and triumphant, and asks what their revolts changed, whether they won or lost.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a> · <a href="/start">the Strategist</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/spartacus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spartacus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Person · d. 71 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Spartacus</span><span class="path-step-why">The gladiator whose army of the enslaved shook Rome for two years.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vercingetorix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 82–46 BCE</span><span class="path-step-name">Vercingetorix</span><span class="path-step-why">The chief who united Gaul against Caesar, and paid for it in a Roman triumph.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/arminius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arminius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Person · c. 17 BCE – 21 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Arminius</span><span class="path-step-why">The Roman-trained officer who annihilated three legions and fixed the empire's frontier at the Rhine.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/boudica"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boudica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Person · d. 60 or 61</span><span class="path-step-name">Boudica</span><span class="path-step-why">The queen whose revolt burned three Roman towns before it broke.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/tupac-amaru-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tupac-amaru-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1738–1781</span><span class="path-step-name">Túpac Amaru II</span><span class="path-step-why">The Andean rising of 1780 that shook Spanish Peru to its foundations.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/toussaint-louverture"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toussaint-louverture.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Person · 1743–1803</span><span class="path-step-name">Toussaint Louverture</span><span class="path-step-why">The general of the enslaved who defeated three empires and made Haiti possible.</span></span></a></li></ol>
